                  /////                              \\\\
              ////       trying darkaifactory          \\\\
                  \\\\                              /////
                       \\\\\\\\----...----/////////

Download the Linux x86_64 archive and matching `.sha256` file from the
[latest release](https://github.com/richiejp/darkaifactory/releases/latest).
The sandbox host needs KVM, cgroup v2, `newuidmap`/`newgidmap`, and subordinate
UID/GID ranges. The orchestrator and client do not need KVM.

```sh
sha256sum -c darkaifactory-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz.sha256
tar -xzf darkaifactory-<version>-linux-x86_64.tar.gz
export PATH="$PWD/darkaifactory-<version>-linux-x86_64/bin:$PATH"
test -r /dev/kvm && test -w /dev/kvm
test -f /sys/fs/cgroup/cgroup.controllers
daft cluster up
daft node list
```

`daft cluster up` starts a disposable single-machine cluster and approves its
local identities. Its state is kept in the invoking user's XDG state directory.
Run `daft cluster down` when finished.

See [sandbox egress](docs/usage/egress.md) for the inspected HTTPS transport,
automatic cleartext-HTTP upgrade, trust contract, and failure behaviour.
